{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NHUEXpeNgrkPmTcAsXRWH7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# QuantAgent-uzq — Implementation: Fix TradingScheduler Heartbeat and Scheduler Unit-Test Regressions\n2\t\n3\t**Issue ID:** QuantAgent-uzq  \n4\t**Phase:** implementer  \n5\t**Acceptance tests:** `docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-uzq-AC-fix-scheduler-heartbeat.md`\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## Root Cause Analysis\n10\t\n11\t### Problem 1 — Missing heartbeat methods in `TradingScheduler`\n12\t\n13\tThe `SchedulerHeartbeat` model (`quantagent/models.py:375`) and its tests (`tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py`) were written expecting two private methods on `TradingScheduler`:\n14\t\n15\t- `_upsert_heartbeat_start(started_at: datetime) -> Optional[SchedulerHeartbeat]`\n16\t- `_upsert_heartbeat_complete(heartbeat: Optional[SchedulerHeartbeat], stats: dict) -> None`\n17\t\n18\tThese methods were never added to `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py`. The `analyze_and_trade()` method (line 148) also never calls them.\n19\t\n20\t### Problem 2 — `DummySession.query()` returns an incomplete mock chain\n21\t\n22\t`PositionMonitor.get_active_position()` (`quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py:26-36`) chains:\n23\t```python\n24\tself.db.query(ActivePosition).filter(...).filter(...).order_by(ActivePosition.id).first()\n25\t```\n26\t\n27\t`DummySession.query()` in `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py` (line 48-53) configures:\n28\t```python\n29\tmock_query.filter.return_value.first.return_value = None\n30\tmock_query.filter.return_value.all.return_value = []\n31\t```\n32\t\n33\tBut does **not** configure `filter.return_value.order_by.return_value.first.return_value`. Because `order_by()` returns an unconfigured `Mock`, calling `.first()` on it returns a truthy `Mock` object instead of `None`.\n34\t\n35\tThis causes `if position:` in `_process_asset()` to be `True`, leading to `update_candle_tracking()` being called on the mock position, which fails with:\n36\t```\n37\tTypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +=: 'Mock' and 'int'\n38\t```\n39\tat `position.candles_since_entry += 1`.\n40\t\n41\tThe exception is caught by the bare `except Exception:` handler in `analyze_and_trade()`, incrementing `errors` instead of `processed`.\n42\t\n43\t---\n44\t\n45\t## Changes Required\n46\t\n47\t### Change 1: `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py`\n48\t\n49\t#### 1a. Add import for `SchedulerHeartbeat`\n50\t\n51\tAdd `SchedulerHeartbeat` to the existing `from quantagent.models import ...` line (line 16).\n52\t\n53\t**Before:**\n54\t```python\n55\tfrom quantagent.models import Environment, Signal, TradeSignal\n56\t```\n57\t\n58\t**After:**\n59\t```python\n60\tfrom quantagent.models import Environment, SchedulerHeartbeat, Signal, TradeSignal\n61\t```\n62\t\n63\t#### 1b. Add `_upsert_heartbeat_start` method\n64\t\n65\tAdd after the `_make_thread_id` method (after line 457):\n66\t\n67\t```python\n68\tdef _upsert_heartbeat_start(self, started_at: datetime) -> Optional[\"SchedulerHeartbeat\"]:\n69\t    try:\n70\t        existing = (\n71\t            self.db.query(SchedulerHeartbeat)\n72\t            .filter(SchedulerHeartbeat.environment == self.environment)\n73\t            .order_by(SchedulerHeartbeat.id)\n74\t            .first()\n75\t        )\n76\t        if existing is not None:\n77\t            existing.timestamp = started_at\n78\t            existing.status = \"running\"\n79\t            existing.assets = list(self.config.assets)\n80\t            self.db.commit()\n81\t            self.db.refresh(existing)\n82\t            return existing\n83\t\n84\t        hb = SchedulerHeartbeat(\n85\t            timestamp=started_at,\n86\t            status=\"running\",\n87\t            environment=self.environment,\n88\t            assets=list(self.config.assets),\n89\t        )\n90\t        self.db.add(hb)\n91\t        self.db.commit()\n92\t        self.db.refresh(hb)\n93\t        return hb\n94\t    except Exception:\n95\t        logger.exception(\"Heartbeat start failed; continuing cycle\")\n96\t        return None\n97\t```\n98\t\n99\t**Contract:**\n100\t- One row per environment — if a row already exists for `self.environment`, update it in place (upsert).\n101\t- Returns `None` on any DB failure; callers must handle this gracefully.\n102\t\n103\t#### 1c. Add `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` method\n104\t\n105\tAdd after `_upsert_heartbeat_start`:\n106\t\n107\t```python\n108\tdef _upsert_heartbeat_complete(\n109\t    self, heartbeat: Optional[\"SchedulerHeartbeat\"], stats: Dict[str, float]\n110\t) -> None:\n111\t    if heartbeat is None:\n112\t        return\n113\t    try:\n114\t        from quantagent.models import Trade\n115\t        last_trade = (\n116\t            self.db.query(Trade)\n117\t            .order_by(Trade.id.desc())\n118\t            .first()\n119\t        )\n120\t        heartbeat.status = \"completed\"\n121\t        heartbeat.completed_at = datetime.utcnow()\n122\t        heartbeat.stats = stats\n123\t        heartbeat.last_trade_id = last_trade.id if last_trade else None\n124\t        self.db.commit()\n125\t    except Exception:\n126\t        logger.exception(\"Heartbeat complete failed\")\n127\t```\n128\t\n129\t**Contract:**\n130\t- No-op when `heartbeat is None` (graceful degradation when start failed).\n131\t- Sets `last_trade_id` to the globally most-recent trade's id (not filtered by environment — consistent with the test expectation in AC-2).\n132\t\n133\t#### 1d. Modify `analyze_and_trade` to call heartbeat methods\n134\t\n135\tWrap the existing method body with heartbeat calls:\n136\t\n137\t**Before (line 148-226):**\n138\t```python\n139\tdef analyze_and_trade(self) -> Dict[str, float]:\n140\t    cycle_start = datetime.utcnow()\n141\t    processed = 0\n142\t    errors = 0\n143\t\n144\t    for symbol in self.config.assets:\n145\t        ...\n146\t\n147\t    duration = (datetime.utcnow() - cycle_start).total_seconds()\n148\t    stats = { ... }\n149\t    self.last_run_stats = stats\n150\t\n151\t    logger.info(...)\n152\t    return stats\n153\t```\n154\t\n155\t**After:**\n156\t```python\n157\tdef analyze_and_trade(self) -> Dict[str, float]:\n158\t    cycle_start = datetime.utcnow()\n159\t    processed = 0\n160\t    errors = 0\n161\t\n162\t    heartbeat = self._upsert_heartbeat_start(cycle_start)  # ADD\n163\t\n164\t    for symbol in self.config.assets:\n165\t        ...\n166\t\n167\t    duration = (datetime.utcnow() - cycle_start).total_seconds()\n168\t    stats = { ... }\n169\t    self.last_run_stats = stats\n170\t\n171\t    self._upsert_heartbeat_complete(heartbeat, stats)  # ADD\n172\t\n173\t    logger.info(...)\n174\t    return stats\n175\t```\n176\t\n177\tThe `heartbeat` call is made before the asset loop; `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` is called after `last_run_stats` is set but before the final `logger.info`.\n178\t\n179\t---\n180\t\n181\t### Change 2: `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py`\n182\t\n183\t#### 2a. Fix `DummySession.query()` mock chain\n184\t\n185\tThe current mock only configures `.filter(...).first()`. It needs to also handle `.filter(...).order_by(...).first()` and `.order_by(...).first()` (used by `_upsert_heartbeat_complete`).\n186\t\n187\t**Before:**\n188\t```python\n189\tdef query(self, model):\n190\t    \"\"\"Return a mock query object that returns no active positions.\"\"\"\n191\t    mock_query = Mock()\n192\t    mock_query.filter.return_value.first.return_value = None\n193\t    mock_query.filter.return_value.all.return_value = []\n194\t    return mock_query\n195\t```\n196\t\n197\t**After:**\n198\t```python\n199\tdef query(self, model):\n200\t    \"\"\"Return a mock query object that returns no results.\"\"\"\n201\t    mock_q = Mock()\n202\t    mock_q.filter.return_value = mock_q\n203\t    mock_q.order_by.return_value = mock_q\n204\t    mock_q.first.return_value = None\n205\t    mock_q.all.return_value = []\n206\t    return mock_q\n207\t```\n208\t\n209\t**Why this works:** The mock becomes self-referential for all chainable methods (`filter`, `order_by`), so any call sequence ending in `.first()` returns `None` and `.all()` returns `[]`. This covers:\n210\t- `query(M).filter(...).order_by(...).first()` → `None` (fixes AC-6, AC-7, AC-8)\n211\t- `query(M).filter(...).first()` → `None` (backwards compatible)\n212\t- `query(M).order_by(...).first()` → `None` (needed by `_upsert_heartbeat_complete`)\n213\t\n214\t---\n215\t\n216\t## Files to Modify\n217\t\n218\t| File | Change type | Lines affected |\n219\t|------|------------|----------------|\n220\t| `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py` | Add 2 methods + modify `analyze_and_trade` | ~458–475 (new methods), ~148–227 (modify) |\n221\t| `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py` | Fix `DummySession.query()` | lines 48–53 |\n222\t\n223\t## Files NOT to Touch\n224\t\n225\t- `quantagent/models.py` — `SchedulerHeartbeat` model is correct as-is\n226\t- `quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py` — no changes needed\n227\t- `tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py` — tests are correct; implementation must match\n228\t- `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml` — out of scope\n229\t\n230\t---\n231\t\n232\t## Verification Commands\n233\t\n234\t```bash\n235\t# Focused gate (8 failing tests)\n236\tDATABASE_URL=postgresql://test:test@localhost:5432/quantagent_test \\\n237\t  /mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python \\\n238\t  -m pytest tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py tests/trading/test_scheduler.py \\\n239\t  -v --tb=short --maxfail=10 -m \"not integration and not slow\"\n240\t\n241\t# Quick check without PostgreSQL (SQLite fallback)\n242\t/mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python \\\n243\t  -m pytest tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py tests/trading/test_scheduler.py \\\n244\t  -v --tb=short -m \"not integration and not slow\"\n245\t```\n246\t\n247\tExpected: all previously-failing tests now show `PASSED`.\n248\t\n249\t---\n250\t\n251\t## Risk Assessment\n252\t\n253\t| Risk | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n254\t|------|-----------|------------|\n255\t| `_upsert_heartbeat_start` race condition on upsert | Low (single-threaded scheduler) | Acceptable; no unique constraint needed |\n256\t| DummySession change breaks currently-passing tests | Low | Self-referential mock is backwards-compatible for all prior patterns |\n257\t| `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` importing `Trade` inline causes circular import | Very low | `Trade` is in `models.py`, already imported elsewhere in scheduler |\n258\t| Heartbeat writes slow down scheduler cycle | Very low | Commit only 2 extra rows per cycle |\n259\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e388d92c-4a3f-4545-9d52-960b86d84a6e","uuid":"4ac8df7b-5e29-4828-90e7-c1f55771a9cc","timestamp":"2026-05-09T07:37:40.896Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/06_implementation/QuantAgent-uzq-IM-fix-scheduler-heartbeat.md","content":"# QuantAgent-uzq — Implementation: Fix TradingScheduler Heartbeat and Scheduler Unit-Test Regressions\n\n**Issue ID:** QuantAgent-uzq  \n**Phase:** implementer  \n**Acceptance tests:** `docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-uzq-AC-fix-scheduler-heartbeat.md`\n\n---\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\n\n### Problem 1 — Missing heartbeat methods in `TradingScheduler`\n\nThe `SchedulerHeartbeat` model (`quantagent/models.py:375`) and its tests (`tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py`) were written expecting two private methods on `TradingScheduler`:\n\n- `_upsert_heartbeat_start(started_at: datetime) -> Optional[SchedulerHeartbeat]`\n- `_upsert_heartbeat_complete(heartbeat: Optional[SchedulerHeartbeat], stats: dict) -> None`\n\nThese methods were never added to `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py`. The `analyze_and_trade()` method (line 148) also never calls them.\n\n### Problem 2 — `DummySession.query()` returns an incomplete mock chain\n\n`PositionMonitor.get_active_position()` (`quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py:26-36`) chains:\n```python\nself.db.query(ActivePosition).filter(...).filter(...).order_by(ActivePosition.id).first()\n```\n\n`DummySession.query()` in `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py` (line 48-53) configures:\n```python\nmock_query.filter.return_value.first.return_value = None\nmock_query.filter.return_value.all.return_value = []\n```\n\nBut does **not** configure `filter.return_value.order_by.return_value.first.return_value`. Because `order_by()` returns an unconfigured `Mock`, calling `.first()` on it returns a truthy `Mock` object instead of `None`.\n\nThis causes `if position:` in `_process_asset()` to be `True`, leading to `update_candle_tracking()` being called on the mock position, which fails with:\n```\nTypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +=: 'Mock' and 'int'\n```\nat `position.candles_since_entry += 1`.\n\nThe exception is caught by the bare `except Exception:` handler in `analyze_and_trade()`, incrementing `errors` instead of `processed`.\n\n---\n\n## Changes Required\n\n### Change 1: `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py`\n\n#### 1a. Add import for `SchedulerHeartbeat`\n\nAdd `SchedulerHeartbeat` to the existing `from quantagent.models import ...` line (line 16).\n\n**Before:**\n```python\nfrom quantagent.models import Environment, Signal, TradeSignal\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nfrom quantagent.models import Environment, SchedulerHeartbeat, Signal, TradeSignal\n```\n\n#### 1b. Add `_upsert_heartbeat_start` method\n\nAdd after the `_make_thread_id` method (after line 457):\n\n```python\ndef _upsert_heartbeat_start(self, started_at: datetime) -> Optional[\"SchedulerHeartbeat\"]:\n    try:\n        existing = (\n            self.db.query(SchedulerHeartbeat)\n            .filter(SchedulerHeartbeat.environment == self.environment)\n            .order_by(SchedulerHeartbeat.id)\n            .first()\n        )\n        if existing is not None:\n            existing.timestamp = started_at\n            existing.status = \"running\"\n            existing.assets = list(self.config.assets)\n            self.db.commit()\n            self.db.refresh(existing)\n            return existing\n\n        hb = SchedulerHeartbeat(\n            timestamp=started_at,\n            status=\"running\",\n            environment=self.environment,\n            assets=list(self.config.assets),\n        )\n        self.db.add(hb)\n        self.db.commit()\n        self.db.refresh(hb)\n        return hb\n    except Exception:\n        logger.exception(\"Heartbeat start failed; continuing cycle\")\n        return None\n```\n\n**Contract:**\n- One row per environment — if a row already exists for `self.environment`, update it in place (upsert).\n- Returns `None` on any DB failure; callers must handle this gracefully.\n\n#### 1c. Add `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` method\n\nAdd after `_upsert_heartbeat_start`:\n\n```python\ndef _upsert_heartbeat_complete(\n    self, heartbeat: Optional[\"SchedulerHeartbeat\"], stats: Dict[str, float]\n) -> None:\n    if heartbeat is None:\n        return\n    try:\n        from quantagent.models import Trade\n        last_trade = (\n            self.db.query(Trade)\n            .order_by(Trade.id.desc())\n            .first()\n        )\n        heartbeat.status = \"completed\"\n        heartbeat.completed_at = datetime.utcnow()\n        heartbeat.stats = stats\n        heartbeat.last_trade_id = last_trade.id if last_trade else None\n        self.db.commit()\n    except Exception:\n        logger.exception(\"Heartbeat complete failed\")\n```\n\n**Contract:**\n- No-op when `heartbeat is None` (graceful degradation when start failed).\n- Sets `last_trade_id` to the globally most-recent trade's id (not filtered by environment — consistent with the test expectation in AC-2).\n\n#### 1d. Modify `analyze_and_trade` to call heartbeat methods\n\nWrap the existing method body with heartbeat calls:\n\n**Before (line 148-226):**\n```python\ndef analyze_and_trade(self) -> Dict[str, float]:\n    cycle_start = datetime.utcnow()\n    processed = 0\n    errors = 0\n\n    for symbol in self.config.assets:\n        ...\n\n    duration = (datetime.utcnow() - cycle_start).total_seconds()\n    stats = { ... }\n    self.last_run_stats = stats\n\n    logger.info(...)\n    return stats\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\ndef analyze_and_trade(self) -> Dict[str, float]:\n    cycle_start = datetime.utcnow()\n    processed = 0\n    errors = 0\n\n    heartbeat = self._upsert_heartbeat_start(cycle_start)  # ADD\n\n    for symbol in self.config.assets:\n        ...\n\n    duration = (datetime.utcnow() - cycle_start).total_seconds()\n    stats = { ... }\n    self.last_run_stats = stats\n\n    self._upsert_heartbeat_complete(heartbeat, stats)  # ADD\n\n    logger.info(...)\n    return stats\n```\n\nThe `heartbeat` call is made before the asset loop; `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` is called after `last_run_stats` is set but before the final `logger.info`.\n\n---\n\n### Change 2: `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py`\n\n#### 2a. Fix `DummySession.query()` mock chain\n\nThe current mock only configures `.filter(...).first()`. It needs to also handle `.filter(...).order_by(...).first()` and `.order_by(...).first()` (used by `_upsert_heartbeat_complete`).\n\n**Before:**\n```python\ndef query(self, model):\n    \"\"\"Return a mock query object that returns no active positions.\"\"\"\n    mock_query = Mock()\n    mock_query.filter.return_value.first.return_value = None\n    mock_query.filter.return_value.all.return_value = []\n    return mock_query\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\ndef query(self, model):\n    \"\"\"Return a mock query object that returns no results.\"\"\"\n    mock_q = Mock()\n    mock_q.filter.return_value = mock_q\n    mock_q.order_by.return_value = mock_q\n    mock_q.first.return_value = None\n    mock_q.all.return_value = []\n    return mock_q\n```\n\n**Why this works:** The mock becomes self-referential for all chainable methods (`filter`, `order_by`), so any call sequence ending in `.first()` returns `None` and `.all()` returns `[]`. This covers:\n- `query(M).filter(...).order_by(...).first()` → `None` (fixes AC-6, AC-7, AC-8)\n- `query(M).filter(...).first()` → `None` (backwards compatible)\n- `query(M).order_by(...).first()` → `None` (needed by `_upsert_heartbeat_complete`)\n\n---\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n| File | Change type | Lines affected |\n|------|------------|----------------|\n| `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py` | Add 2 methods + modify `analyze_and_trade` | ~458–475 (new methods), ~148–227 (modify) |\n| `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py` | Fix `DummySession.query()` | lines 48–53 |\n\n## Files NOT to Touch\n\n- `quantagent/models.py` — `SchedulerHeartbeat` model is correct as-is\n- `quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py` — no changes needed\n- `tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py` — tests are correct; implementation must match\n- `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml` — out of scope\n\n---\n\n## Verification Commands\n\n```bash\n# Focused gate (8 failing tests)\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://test:test@localhost:5432/quantagent_test \\\n  /mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python \\\n  -m pytest tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py tests/trading/test_scheduler.py \\\n  -v --tb=short --maxfail=10 -m \"not integration and not slow\"\n\n# Quick check without PostgreSQL (SQLite fallback)\n/mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python \\\n  -m pytest tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py tests/trading/test_scheduler.py \\\n  -v --tb=short -m \"not integration and not slow\"\n```\n\nExpected: all previously-failing tests now show `PASSED`.\n\n---\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n| Risk | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|------|-----------|------------|\n| `_upsert_heartbeat_start` race condition on upsert | Low (single-threaded scheduler) | Acceptable; no unique constraint needed |\n| DummySession change breaks currently-passing tests | Low | Self-referential mock is backwards-compatible for all prior patterns |\n| `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` importing `Trade` inline causes circular import | Very low | `Trade` is in `models.py`, already imported elsewhere in scheduler |\n| Heartbeat writes slow down scheduler cycle | Very low | Commit only 2 extra rows per cycle |\n","numLines":259,"startLine":1,"totalLines":259}}}
